# Implementation Plan: Eliminate Dummy Dates & Transition Mock Data to Dynamic / Clean States

Update all hardcoded static dates (e.g., `'2026-10-03'`, `'12 Sep 2026'`) to live dynamic timestamps relative to the current real-time system clock, and transition mock/sample records across the dashboard to clean, user-driven, or persistent local storage states.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - All date pickers (such as Port Prediction Laycan Date) will now dynamically default to a realistic forward-looking commercial date (e.g. today + 14 days in `YYYY-MM-DD`) calculated at runtime using `new Date()`.
> - The Tracking Search and History panels will support clean empty states when no user searches exist, rather than forcing static dummy history.
> - Any reference demo voyages will compute real-time relative departure, current waypoint, and ETA timestamps dynamically (e.g. `Departed 2 days ago`, `ETA in 4 days`).
> - Copyright & legal notices will use `new Date().getFullYear()` and dynamic current month/year strings.

